Build a grounding gate that refuses out-of-knowledge questions before the model is ever called Prompt the …

Welcome to Loop Patterns and Anti-Patterns. By now you can run a loop and stop it safely. The skill this module adds is judgment: instead of improvising a loop from scratch every time, you&amp;rsquo;ll recognize the situation and reach for a proven shape. Named patterns are how experienced people move fast — you see a task and think &amp;ldquo;that&amp;rsquo;s a generate-and-test&amp;rdquo; the way a cook sees ingredients and thinks &amp;ldquo;that&amp;rsquo;s a stir-fry.&amp;rdquo;
You&amp;rsquo;ll learn four workhorse patterns. Draft, critique, revise is the everyday loop you&amp;rsquo;ve been building since Module 3. Plan then execute breaks a big task into a plan first, then runs a small loop for each step. Generate and test produces several candidates and picks the best against your check. Parallel loops and handoffs split work across more than one pass or more than one agent. For each, you&amp;rsquo;ll learn what it&amp;rsquo;s good at and where it falls down.
